instruction":"Identify the process goal, actors, inputs and expected outcome.","reason":"A clear process prevents incorrect work.","student_check":"Can you explain the goal in one sentence?"},{"step_number":2,"title":"Apply","instruction":"Complete this workplace lab: Describe a project disagreement resolved through an agreed test.","reason":"Hands-on execution turns knowledge into a reusable skill.","student_check":"Did you complete every required part?"},{"step_number":3,"title":"Validate","instruction":"Test the result, review the evidence and correct any gap.","reason":"Validation makes the work reliable and interview-ready.","student_check":"Does the result satisfy the stated outcome?"}],"use_when":"Use this workflow for assess work.","do_not_use_when":"Do not expose confidential information or skip verification.","faster_method":"Avoid this common mistake: Using hypotheticals or saying only what the team did."},"worked_examples":[{"example_number":1,"title":"Guided practice","difficulty":"Foundation to applied","question_or_scenario":"Complete this workplace lab: Describe a project disagreement resolved through an agreed test.","given_information":["STAR Method","Behavioural Questions"],"reasoning_steps":[{"step_number":1,"explanation":"Review the assess requirements and define the expected result."},{"step_number":2,"explanation":"Describe a project disagreement resolved through an agreed test."},{"step_number":3,"explanation":"Validate the outcome. Avoid this common mistake: Using hypotheticals or saying only what the team did."}],"final_answer":"A complete submission uses STAR Method checklist and evidence log, follows the workflow, records validation evidence and explains one limitation.","why_the_answer_is_correct":"The result follows the defined process, covers the required elements and includes a validation step.","learning_takeaway":"Avoid this common mistake: Using hypotheticals or saying only what the team did."}],"usage_comparisons":[],"common_mistakes":[{"mistake_number":1,"title":"Acting before understanding","incorrect_approach":"Starting immediately without confirming scope, inputs and success criteria.","why_students_make_it":"Speed can feel more important than process discipline.","why_it_is_wrong":"An incomplete process creates unreliable results and avoidable rework.","correction":"Define the outcome, complete the workflow, and validate it once.","prevention_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Using hypotheticals or saying only what the team did."}],"memory_support":{"memory_aid":"Avoid this common mistake: Using hypotheticals or saying only what the team did.","mental_model":"Concept → Practice → Proof","quick_recall_note":"Understand → Apply → Validate"},"placement_support":{"question_identification_signals":["Assess","STAR Method: Workplace Lab & Module Check","STAR Method","Behavioural Questions"],"time_management_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Using hypotheticals or saying only what the team did.","exam_traps":["Skipping context","Ignoring edge cases or validation"],"interview_relevance":"Use the completed activity and its validation evidence to explain your approach in interviews."},"checkpoint_questions":[{"question_number":1,"type":"application","question":"In your own words, what problem does star method solve?","answer":"Behavioural answers show judgement through situation, personal action, result and learning.","explanation":"A strong answer states the business or user problem before naming a tool.","skill_tested":"STAR Method: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":2,"type":"reasoning","question":"How would you apply this capability in the following workplace situation: Describe a project disagreement resolved through an agreed test.","answer":"Define the purpose and audience, gather verified facts, apply the STAR Method method, check the result, and record the next action.","explanation":"The response should describe a controlled, verifiable workflow rather than only a feature.","skill_tested":"STAR Method: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":3,"type":"application","question":"Explain how you would apply star method in this scenario: Describe a project disagreement resolved through an agreed test.","answer":"Use Behavioural answers show judgement through situation, personal action, result and learning. Then describe the workflow: Define the purpose and audience, gather verified facts, apply the STAR Method method, check the result, and record the next action.","explanation":"Interview answers should connect principle, action, validation and outcome.","skill_tested":"STAR Method: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":4,"type":"application","question":"Identify the main risk in this incorrect approach: Using hypotheticals or saying only what the team did.","answer":"The approach is unreliable because it breaks the controls implied by Behavioural answers show judgement through situation, personal action, result and learning.","explanation":"The correction should address cause and verification, not only appearance.","skill_tested":"STAR Method: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":5,"type":"application","question":"Which tool or artefact would you use first, and what would you verify?","answer":"Use STAR Method checklist and evidence log; verify that the result satisfies the stated decision, data and quality requirements.","explanation":"Tools support a method; they do not replace validation.","skill_tested":"STAR Method: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"}],"remediation":{"likely_confusion":"The concept may feel abstract before it is connected to a practical workflow.","simplified_explanation":"Apply Behavioural answers show judgement through situation, personal action, result and learning. Complete the scenario, produce evidence, explain the decision and correct the common failure: Using hypotheticals or saying only what the team did.","simple_example":"Describe a project disagreement resolved through an agreed test.","prerequisite_to_review":"Assess","next_recommended_step":"Complete this workplace lab: Describe a project disagreement resolved through an agreed test."},"revision_asset":{"summary":"Apply Behavioural answers show judgement through situation, personal action, result and learning. Complete the scenario, produce evidence, explain the decision and correct the common failure: Using hypotheticals or saying only what the team did.","key_points":["STAR Method","Behavioural Questions","Avoid this common mistake: Using hypotheticals or saying only what the team did."],"one_minute_revision":"STAR Method: Workplace Lab & Module Check: Apply Behavioural answers show judgement through situation, personal action, result and learning. Complete the scenario, produce evidence, explain the decision and correct the common failure: Using hypotheticals or saying only what the team did.","final_checklist":["I can explain the concept.","I can complete the activity.","I can validate and present the result."]},"quality_metadata":{"content_origin":"taksh_authored","review_status":"approved","copyright_review_status":"original","prompt_version":"deterministic-v2","generated_by":"taksh","sections_not_applicable":[]}}'::jsonb,content_version=content_version+1,reviewed_at=now(),approved_at=now(),published_at=now(),skill_tags=array['STAR Method','Behavioural Questions']::text[],updated_at=now() where course='Interview Skills & Personal Branding' and module='Module 4 · STAR Method' and topic='Assess' and subtopic='STAR Method: Workplace Lab & Module Check' and status<>'archived';

