s the required elements and includes a validation step.","learning_takeaway":"Avoid this common mistake: Memorising one answer for every role."}],"usage_comparisons":[],"common_mistakes":[{"mistake_number":1,"title":"Acting before understanding","incorrect_approach":"Starting immediately without confirming scope, inputs and success criteria.","why_students_make_it":"Speed can feel more important than process discipline.","why_it_is_wrong":"An incomplete process creates unreliable results and avoidable rework.","correction":"Define the outcome, complete the workflow, and validate it once.","prevention_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Memorising one answer for every role."}],"memory_support":{"memory_aid":"Avoid this common mistake: Memorising one answer for every role.","mental_model":"Concept → Practice → Proof","quick_recall_note":"Understand → Apply → Validate"},"placement_support":{"question_identification_signals":["Assess","Mock Interview Capstone: Workplace Lab & Module Check","Interview Practice","Follow-up"],"time_management_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Memorising one answer for every role.","exam_traps":["Skipping context","Ignoring edge cases or validation"],"interview_relevance":"Use the completed activity and its validation evidence to explain your approach in interviews."},"checkpoint_questions":[{"question_number":1,"type":"application","question":"In your own words, what problem does mock interview capstone solve?","answer":"Interview readiness combines concise evidence, listening, professional questions and follow-up.","explanation":"A strong answer states the business or user problem before naming a tool.","skill_tested":"Mock Interview Capstone: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":2,"type":"reasoning","question":"How would you apply this capability in the following workplace situation: Complete a mock interview from introduction through candidate questions.","answer":"Define the purpose and audience, gather verified facts, apply the Interview Practice method, check the result, and record the next action.","explanation":"The response should describe a controlled, verifiable workflow rather than only a feature.","skill_tested":"Mock Interview Capstone: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":3,"type":"application","question":"Explain how you would apply interview practice in this scenario: Complete a mock interview from introduction through candidate questions.","answer":"Use Interview readiness combines concise evidence, listening, professional questions and follow-up. Then describe the workflow: Define the purpose and audience, gather verified facts, apply the Interview Practice method, check the result, and record the next action.","explanation":"Interview answers should connect principle, action, validation and outcome.","skill_tested":"Mock Interview Capstone: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":4,"type":"application","question":"Identify the main risk in this incorrect approach: Memorising one answer for every role.","answer":"The approach is unreliable because it breaks the controls implied by Interview readiness combines concise evidence, listening, professional questions and follow-up.","explanation":"The correction should address cause and verification, not only appearance.","skill_tested":"Mock Interview Capstone: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":5,"type":"application","question":"Which tool or artefact would you use first, and what would you verify?","answer":"Use Mock Interview Capstone checklist and evidence log; verify that the result satisfies the stated decision, data and quality requirements.","explanation":"Tools support a method; they do not replace validation.","skill_tested":"Mock Interview Capstone: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"}],"remediation":{"li