alue."}],"usage_comparisons":[],"common_mistakes":[{"mistake_number":1,"title":"Acting before understanding","incorrect_approach":"Starting immediately without confirming scope, inputs and success criteria.","why_students_make_it":"Speed can feel more important than process discipline.","why_it_is_wrong":"An incomplete process creates unreliable results and avoidable rework.","correction":"Define the outcome, complete the workflow, and validate it once.","prevention_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Writing vague notes or chasing without value."}],"memory_support":{"memory_aid":"Avoid this common mistake: Writing vague notes or chasing without value.","mental_model":"Concept → Practice → Proof","quick_recall_note":"Understand → Apply → Validate"},"placement_support":{"question_identification_signals":["Apply","CRM and Relationships: Practical Workflow","CRM","Relationship Building"],"time_management_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Writing vague notes or chasing without value.","exam_traps":["Skipping context","Ignoring edge cases or validation"],"interview_relevance":"Use the completed activity and its validation evidence to explain your approach in interviews."},"checkpoint_questions":[{"question_number":1,"type":"application","question":"In your own words, what problem does crm and relationships solve?","answer":"Reliable sales work depends on accurate records, dated actions and useful post-sale communication.","explanation":"A strong answer states the business or user problem before naming a tool.","skill_tested":"CRM and Relationships: Practical Workflow","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":2,"type":"reasoning","question":"How would you apply this capability in the following workplace situation: Record stakeholders, need, risk and next step after discovery.","answer":"Define the purpose and audience, gather verified facts, apply the CRM method, check the result, and record the next action.","explanation":"The response should describe a contr