ear students with different messages for discovery, evaluation and enrolment."},{"step_number":3,"explanation":"Validate the outcome. Avoid this common mistake: Choosing channels because they are popular rather than because they fit audience and objective."}],"final_answer":"A complete submission uses Campaign brief and funnel map, follows the workflow, records validation evidence and explains one limitation.","why_the_answer_is_correct":"The result follows the defined process, covers the required elements and includes a validation step.","learning_takeaway":"Avoid this common mistake: Choosing channels because they are popular rather than because they fit audience and objective."}],"usage_comparisons":[],"common_mistakes":[{"mistake_number":1,"title":"Acting before understanding","incorrect_approach":"Starting immediately without confirming scope, inputs and success criteria.","why_students_make_it":"Speed can feel more important than process discipline.","why_it_is_wrong":"An incomplete process creates unreliable results and avoidable rework.","correction":"Define the outcome, complete the workflow, and validate it once.","prevention_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Choosing channels because they are popular rather than because they fit audience and objective."}],"memory_support":{"memory_aid":"Avoid this common mistake: Choosing channels because they are popular rather than because they fit audience and objective.","mental_model":"Concept → Practice → Proof","quick_recall_note":"Understand → Apply → Validate"},"placement_support":{"question_identification_signals":["Assess","Marketing Strategy and Funnel: Workplace Lab & Module Check","Digital Marketing","Marketing Funnel"],"time_management_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Choosing channels because they are popular rather than because they fit audience and objective.","exam_traps":["Skipping context","Ignoring edge cases or validation"],"interview_relevance":"Use the completed activity and its validation evidence to explain your approach in interviews."},"checkpoint_questions":[{"question_number":1,"type":"application","question":"In your own words, what problem does marketing strategy and funnel solve?","answer":"Digital marketing connects a defined audience and value proposition to measurable acquisition, conversion and retention outcomes.","explanation":"A strong answer states the business or user problem before naming a tool.","skill_tested":"Marketing Strategy and Funnel: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation"},{"question_number":2,"type":"reasoning","question":"How would you apply this capability in the following workplace situation: A training programme targets final-year students with different messages for discovery, evaluation and enrolment.","answer":"Set the business goal, research the audience, state the offer, map funnel stages and choose metrics before channels.","explanation":"The response should describe a controlled, verifiable workflow rather than only a feature.","skill_tested":"Marketing Strategy and Funnel: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation"},{"question_number":3,"type":"application","question":"Differentiate awareness, consideration and conversion metrics.","answer":"Use Digital marketing connects a defined audience and value proposition to measurable acquisition, conversion and retention outcomes. Then describe the workflow: Set the business goal, research the audience, state the offer, map funnel stages and choose metrics before channels.","explanation":"Interview answers should connect principle, action, validation and outcome.","skill_tested":"Marketing Strategy and Funnel: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation"},{"question_number":4,"type":"application","question":"Identify the main risk in this incorrect approach: Choosing channels because they are popular rather than because they fit audience and objective.","answer":"The approach is unreliable because it breaks the controls implied by Digi